<p>Several vessels linked to France, Japan, and Oman crossed the Strait of Hormuz from Thursday into Friday, marking some of the first confirmed transits by those operators since the Iran war sharply curtailed traffic through the waterway. Ship-tracking data cited by multiple outlets showed the French-owned CMA CGM Kribi exiting the strait on Friday after departing Dubai. A Japanese-linked gas carrier and several Omani-operated tankers also made the passage. The crossings point to a limited reopening under Iran’s stated policy of allowing vessels it considers friendly and free of US or Israeli links to transit. Iran had effectively shut the strait after US and Israeli airstrikes at the end of February widened the conflict, disrupting a route that carries about a fifth of global oil and LNG flows and contributing to fuel shortages and higher energy prices worldwide. Iran also said it is drafting a peacetime protocol with Oman to supervise maritime traffic after the war ends, a possible sign that both sides are trying to restore more predictable shipping rules.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/EM4TYHgFCgeo8JfmQCOKG_YBKbv3yyZxaKLybjQ6TkLVfZw-40n2HfhsZpsspfLV66k_XOp9yhA9iXqhOEZPEJMaipc57_zCZ0P2uWNhq8FR' alt='Cargo ships in the Gulf, near the Strait of Hormuz, as seen from northern Ras al-Khaimah amid the US-Israeli war on Iran, in United Arab Emirates, March 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>LNG return: The Sohar LNG tanker was the first liquefied natural gas carrier reported to cross the strait since March 1, according to Marine Traffic data cited by Dawn.</li><li>Approved route: Some of the few recent transits used an Iranian-approved passage near Larak Island, which Lloyd’s List dubbed the “Tehran Toll Booth”.</li><li>European first: BBC said the CMA CGM vessel appeared to be the first ship owned by a major European firm to pass through the strait since the conflict began.</li><li>Global chokepoint: The Strait of Hormuz normally handles roughly one-fifth of global oil and LNG flows, so even a limited resumption matters for energy markets and shipping planners.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iran: Iran said it is drafting a peacetime protocol with Oman to supervise maritime traffic through the Strait of Hormuz after the war, with the goal of setting basic rules for ship movements. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988387/four-ships-cross-hormuz-as-iran-says-it-is-drafting-protocol'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Japanese shipping company Mitsui O.S.K. Lines: The company said a liquefied natural gas tanker registered in Japan had crossed the strait for the first time since the Iran war began. (<a href='https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260403-container-ship-declaring-french-ownership-passes-through-hormuz-strait'>France 24</a>)</li><li>Reuters-reported shipping data: Shipping data showed that three Omani-operated tankers, a French-owned container ship, and a Japanese-owned gas carrier crossed from Thursday onward, matching Iran’s policy of allowing passage to vessels it considers friendly. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/japanese-french-and-omani-vessels-cross-strait-hormuz'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3349004/iran-war-french-and-japanese-owned-ships-make-first-strait-hormuz-crossings'>Iran war: French and Japanese-owned ships make first Strait of Hormuz crossings</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/japanese-french-and-omani-vessels-cross-the-strait-of-hormuz'>French and Japanese-owned ships make first Hormuz crossings</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988387/four-ships-cross-hormuz-as-iran-says-it-is-drafting-protocol'>Four ships cross Hormuz as Iran says it is drafting protocol</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-vessels-strait-of-hormuz-iran-war-france-japan-oman/'>Japanese, French and Omani vessels crossed Strait of Hormuz since Thursday, data shows</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/french-japanese-ships-cross-strait-hormuz-first-war'>French, Japanese ships cross Strait of Hormuz in first since war</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cjd8275jrrko'>French-owned ship passes through Strait of Hormuz</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/3/french-owned-container-ship-transits-hormuz-strait-in-first-since-iran-war'>Omani, French and Japanese vessels transit the Strait of Hormuz</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260403-container-ship-declaring-french-ownership-passes-through-hormuz-strait'>Japanese shipping company Mitsui O.S.K. Lines says that a liquefied natural gas oil tanker registered in Japan crosses the Strait of Hormuz for the first since the beginning of the Iran war. A third ship also crosses the strait. (Kyodo News)</a> - france24.com</li></ul>